            <ArticleTitle>Airbag pneumonitis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>498569</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1155/2010/498569</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The widespread and mandatory use of airbags has resulted in various patterns of injuries and complications unique to their use. Airbags have been implicated in a spectrum of pulmonary conditions ranging from exacerbation of asthma, reactive airway diseases to new onset asthma. We report a case of inhalational chemical pneumonitis that developed after exposure to the airbag fumes.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
